# envs/.env  —  MACHINE-SPECIFIC, NON-SECRET values only.
# Copy to envs/.env and fill the two paths below. DO NOT put credentials here —
# all 19 credentials live in Bitwarden Secrets Manager (see docs/bitwarden.secrets.manager.md)
# and are injected at runtime by `bws run` (scripts/bws-config.sh).

# ── non-secret machine paths (safe to keep here) ─────────────────────────
# Quote the values — `make render` sources this file, so an unquoted path with
# spaces would break.
APOLLO_MCP_PATH="/ABSOLUTE/PATH/to/apollo-io-mcp/dist/index.js"
GDRIVE_CREDS_DIR="/ABSOLUTE/PATH/to/gdrive-creds"      # dir holding gcp-oauth.keys.json
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS="/ABSOLUTE/PATH/to/ga-service-account.json"  # GA4 (analytics.readonly); the JSON key itself is a secret on disk — keep it git-ignored

# ── the following are SECRETS — store in Bitwarden, DO NOT add values here ─
# Bitwarden secret KEY must equal the variable name (1:1), so `bws run` exposes it correctly:
#   APOLLO_API_KEY            HUBSPOT_ACCESS_TOKEN     LINKEDIN_COOKIE
#   UPWORK_ACCESS_TOKEN       GDRIVE_CLIENT_ID         GDRIVE_CLIENT_SECRET
#   META_ADS_ACCESS_TOKEN     META_AD_ACCOUNT_ID       META_APP_ID
#   META_APP_SECRET           META_BUSINESS_ID         X_API_KEY
#   X_API_SECRET              X_ACCESS_TOKEN           X_ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET
#   YOUTUBE_API_KEY           GOOGLE_PROJECT_ID        GOOGLE_ADS_DEVELOPER_TOKEN
#   FAL_KEY
#
# New in Task 004 — remotion, excalidraw, playwright, and cloudflare-observability
# servers need NO secrets (Cloudflare uses browser OAuth via mcp-remote on first connect).
# google-analytics reuses GOOGLE_PROJECT_ID (above) + the GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS path.
